For Release 1.0.0 - Nov 23, 2026

    - Forms now use libcurl's MIME API (curl_mime_init and related
      functions) instead of the deprecated curl_formadd API, which has
      been removed entirely.
      - The 'httppost option (CURLOPT_HTTPPOST) is replaced by the new
        'mimepost option (CURLOPT_MIMEPOST).  This is an incompatible
        change: code using 'httppost must switch to 'mimepost.  The list
        of fields it takes is unchanged.
      - The filename of a 4-element field is now sent, so the field is
        uploaded as a file.  It was previously ignored.
      - Fields with an empty value are sent instead of being dropped.
      - A name, MIME type or filename containing NUL raises an error.
    - guile-curl now uses semantic versioning (MAJOR.MINOR.MICRO).
      The shared library's libtool version is 3:0:0, so it is now
      installed as libguile-curl.so.3.
    - New procedures:
      - curl-easy-perform-to-fd streams a response to a file descriptor,
        optionally at a byte offset, while other threads keep running;
        curl-easy-progress reports its progress and curl-easy-cancel!
        stops it.  (Contributed by Nala Ginrut.)
      - curl-easy-send and curl-easy-receive exchange raw data over a
        connect-only connection.
      - curl-easy-header and curl-easy-headers return the response
        headers of the last transfer (libcurl 7.83.0 or later).
      - curl-easy-upkeep performs connection upkeep.
    - About 50 more curl-easy-setopt options, including failonerror,
      ssl-options, pinnedpublickey, protocols-str, tls13-ciphers, hsts,
      altsvc and proxyheader, a new blob type for certificates and keys
      in memory (cainfo-blob, sslcert-blob, sslkey-blob and others), and
      the constants they take.  Setting an option that the installed
      libcurl is too old to have raises an error saying so.
    - New getinfo values: content-type and certinfo.
    - Fix crashes and memory corruption: a stale header callback after
      requests made with headers, the read port being garbage collected
      during uploads, Scheme errors unwinding through libcurl
      callbacks, and handles being freed while the process exits.
    - Fix memory leaks in list (slist) options, getinfo and printing of
      handles.
    - Errors from the C code now raise misc-error with a proper
      message, and curl-easy-setopt reports libcurl's own error.
    - curl-error-code and curl-error-string are now per thread.
    - curl-easy-getinfo works after a failed transfer.
    - Add support for the connect-to option, the speed-upload-t and
      earlydata-sent-t getinfo values, and binary data for
      copypostfields.
    - Options and getinfo values that depend on the libcurl version
      were always disabled, because they were tested with #ifdef but
      libcurl declares them as enums.  Those from libcurl 7.76.0 or
      earlier, such as doh-url and haproxyprotocol, are now always
      available, and newer getinfo values, such as conn-id and xfer-id,
      are available when libcurl is new enough.
    - Much faster collection of large response bodies.
    - When libcurl uses a synchronous DNS resolver, new handles set
      nosignal by default.
    - libcurl 7.76.0 or later is required, and configure checks for it.
    - The check_type test program initializes guile-curl fully and reports
      the test and any Scheme error when it fails, instead of aborting
      silently.
    - The manual explains how to find out why a transfer failed and how
      to fix HTTPS certificate errors without turning off verification.
    - Building from the repository requires gettext, for Guile's
      guile.m4 macros.

For Release 0.9 - Jan 19, 2021

    - Speed up bv->url-encoded-bytevector
    - Improve reliability of parallel builds

For Release 0.8 - Jan 11, 2021

    - Eliminate all traces of gnulib
    - Use srfi-64 for test scripts
    - Avoid recursive automake
    - Simplify build somewhat
    - When CURL constants and enums are not present, the Guile versions
      will be #f, instead of undefined now.
    - Use pkg-config instead of curl-config to gather information
      about the libcurl install
    - Remove ChangeLog

For Release 0.7 - Jan 1, 2021

    - Eliminate Guile 2.0 support
    - Allow Guile 3.0 support
    - Update gnulib

For Release 0.6 - Feb 15, 2019

    - Eliminate Guile 1.8 support
    - Update to libcurl 7.61.x constant
    - guilesitedir become guilemoduledir
    - follow guile-hall's guidance of how guile directories are formed
    - load unversioned libguile-curl library in curl.scm

For Release 0.5 - April 8, 2017

    - Fix configure to search for Guile 2.2.x.

For Release 0.4 - Oct 23, 2016

    - Fix GC with Guile 2.0.12+
    - Add support for readdata option

For Release 0.3 - Oct 2, 2014

    - Fix bad memory allocation for POSTFIELDS
    - More tests

For Release 0.2 - Feb 16, 2013

    - Update to recent curl library
    - Add support for all current options, including those that take
      slist and httppost
    - Fix guile-1.8 and guile-2.0 specific functionality
    - Fixes for i386-unknown-openbsd5.2
    - New debugging function %curl-dump-handle

For Release 0.1

    - Initial release
